  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2009 Nature Physics article has accumulated measurable academic uptake, with 12 citations and a field- and year-normalized standing in the top 10% of cited works. Its record also shows downstream reuse across 12 later works, alongside a small but visible footprint in public and teaching contexts.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Measured measurement by Markus Aspelmeyer is a closed-access journal article that has found a clear audience within quantum physics and related areas. The citation pattern indicates sustained scholarly reuse over time, and the normalized percentile places it among the stronger performers for its publication year and field.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing literature is anchored in quantum mechanics, quantum information, and quantum tomography, which fits the article\u2019s conceptual profile around quantum measurement and state reconstruction. Most downstream uses are articles, with a smaller number of letters, suggesting that the work has been taken up primarily as part of ongoing technical and theoretical development rather than as a one-off reference.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The broader reach record is modest but not empty. There is one Bluesky mention, one additional online mention beyond citations, and one YouTube video that explicitly links the paper in its metadata or description, indicating some visibility outside the formal citation ecosystem. The public-discourse archive was unavailable, so the record here is best read as partial rather than comprehensive.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence shows a paper with steady scholarly resonance and a small but observable presence in online and instructional contexts. The impact signal is concentrated in academic reuse, with the strongest support coming from citation performance and the downstream literature that has built on it.</p>",
